      "side": 1,
      "message": "`max_symbols` shares a table with everything the isolate interns for itself: every symbol constant of every library it loads, record type names, keywords. A host choosing a cap needs to know that baseline, or a cap that seems generous fails isolate creation or the first `(import ...)`.\n\nWorth stating that the cap includes it. Exposing the live count, such as `Cx::symbol_count()`, would let a host set the cap relative to what its isolate starts with.",
      "revId": "07f1ffa7507f67dbac297e16b413cc2c673dd2df",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
