      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"So the isolate is left as it was\" holds for `string-\u003esymbol` and the reader. A module load that reaches the cap partway through its constants leaves the constants already built in the pool (ADR 0020), which never frees. The load fails cleanly, but not without trace. Saying \"fails cleanly, keeping what was already built\" would be exact.",
      "revId": "07f1ffa7507f67dbac297e16b413cc2c673dd2df",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
